        "id": 63212,
        "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-05-17T12:17:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>As much as I hate to say it, as I generally like quirky PvP variant rules, MedicTank is right. &nbsp;Support characters like Argent Adept, Visionary, Legacy, and even Mister Fixer would be at a decided disadvantage, as they have no end-of-game \"nova\" ability, and only deal damage in small, discrete chunks. Even Tempest would be at a disadvantage, as his highest unbuffed &nbsp;attack is what, 7 points? (Lightning Slash with Shackles out)</p><p>Much as it'd be cool to see heroes going against one another--and it's a pretty common comics trope, see also: &nbsp;Civil War, Crisis on Infinite Earths, etc.--SotM just isn't currently set up that way. &nbsp;And when you're fighting against the intrinsic mechanics of the game, that's a battle you're never going to actually win, but just settle on.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:40:01.967Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
