      {
        "id": 63213,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-05-17T18:15:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Sure Tempest can deal at max damage 7 using Lightning Slash and Gene-Bound Shackles, but that isn't the only thing he can do on his turn. Electrical Storm will add another 3 damage and Localized Hurricane will also deal another 5 damage. That is 15 damage in a single turn, not too bad. Argent Adept is also capable of dealing&nbsp;27 damage in a single turn as well. Fixer could get up to 9 damage. Legacy can do 11 damage on his turn as well.</p><p>Really the only hero who would have trouble is Visionary, as she can do 4 damage in a single turn unless she uses both her Twist the Ethers on herself to deal out 9 damage.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Edit: Also to toss in, whenever I play with others I always try to get the killing blow, because it's fun that way! Unless the environment is set-up in a way I can allow that to kill the villain as that is even more fun. Especially when the Final Wasteland is involved.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
